\title{Security Levels in Production}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    [What bit-security a deployed system actually claims](dhsorens-004N), under which assumptions, and who checked. This is where [soundness regimes](dhsorens-0038) stop being a theoretical distinction.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The parameters real provers ship: rate, repetitions, [grinding](dhsorens-003A) bits, field size — and the claimed level they add up to.}
        \li{Which claims depend on a [conjecture](dhsorens-002P), and whether that is documented in the system's own materials.}
        \li{The accounting across [recursion](dhsorens-003L) layers, where errors compose.}
        \li{Who is responsible for the number: protocol designers, implementers, or auditors.}
        \li{What a machine-checked parameter calculation would look like, and whether it is a reasonable thing to build.}
    }
}
